Package: lpu-kmod
Version: @VERSION@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: ThinkNative verification <verify@thinknative.invalid>
Description: ThinkNative LPU AI accelerator kernel module (thin PCIe driver)
 Thin out-of-tree driver for the ThinkNative LPU AI accelerator: exposes
 the BAR0/BAR1 windows (write-combine mmap) and coherent host-memory
 allocations (LPU_IOCTL_GET_INFO / HOST_ALLOC / HOST_FREE) to the
 userspace runtime. No scheduler semantics in kernel space; completion
 is handled by CQ polling per LPU-SCHED-SPEC.md (QEMU verification tree).
 .
 Built against kernel @KVER@. After installing, load with:
   depmod -a @KVER@ && modprobe lpu
 or directly:
   insmod /lib/modules/@KVER@/updates/lpu.ko
 Device nodes appear as /dev/lpu0, /dev/lpu1, ... (misc devices).
